  "method": "the intended turn as early as the finger shows it (DAgger): in every gesture window of the training games the live game's turns give the intended screen directions; the right answer at a tick is the first intended direction not yet reached, relative to David's heading, from the moment the finger movement asking for it is clear (10 dp of travel at 150 dp/s; a second turn answering the same movement: clear at the live turn, asked from when the first was clear), unknown between the movement's start and that moment (no example), none otherwise; a target not reached within 500 ms of its movement's start is dropped. Examples (features, answer) at every tick of the live games, then at every tick the model decides while playing the windows (one round of rollouts per round); the softmax policy is refitted on all examples each round (cross-entropy, L2, Adam) with turn answers weighted w_turn, none answers during a clear finger movement the live game did not answer (for 300 ms) w_reject, and none answers within 400 ms after a turn w_hold",
